<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuku of Tidore</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1738">1738</a>–<a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Nuku, Nuku Muhammad Amiruddin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuku was a prince of Tidore in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a> who led a long revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> from 1780, after the company had interfered in the Tidorese succession. Operating from Seram, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-ampat-islands">Raja Ampat Islands</a> and the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> and aided by the British, he won control of Tidore in the late 1790s and ruled it as sultan until his death in 1805. He is honoured as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuku-of-tidore.jpg" alt="Nuku of Tidore" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuku_Muhammad_Amiruddin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
